From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:36:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Double the DRAM refresh when hot

FSP-M leaves REFRESH_2X_MODE off. JEDEC asks for twice the refresh rate
of DDR4 above 85 C; the SO-DIMMs of the M720q/M920q have no thermal
sensor of their own and sit next to the processor in a small case, and
the M920x of ouroBIOS runs as a server around the clock. Mode 2 doubles
the refresh only when the memory controller finds the DIMMs hot, so
nothing changes at normal temperatures.

The UPD is part of the memory settings, so the version of ouroBIOS's
memory settings goes up and the first boot trains again.
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
index b2ffa7193fe..5228f6bef11 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
@@ -128,6 +128,15 @@ void mainboard_memory_init_params(FSPM_UPD *memupd)
 
 	memupd->FspmConfig.Peg0Enable = peg_enable(memupd);
 
+	/*
+	 * Double the refresh of the DIMMs when the memory controller finds them
+	 * hot: JEDEC asks for it above 85 C, and the SO-DIMMs of this small
+	 * case, with no thermal sensor of their own, sit next to the processor
+	 * of a machine that is often a server. FSP-M leaves it off; at normal
+	 * temperatures nothing changes.
+	 */
+	memupd->FspmConfig.Refresh2X = 2;
+
 	/*
 	 * With the ME disabled (Security > Management Engine), FSP-M's HECI
 	 * messages get no answer on some boots: FspMemoryInit then takes
